---
title: "Grid Layout Test"
---

This is an internal page holding examples that exercise edge cases of [Grid Layout](./grid-size/) - in particular the auto height body height limits - which are useful for manual QA but not instructive enough to belong on the documentation page itself. It is intentionally left out of the site navigation.

## Auto Height with Max Height and Server-Side Row Model

Rows should be loaded in blocks of 100 as you scroll, rather than loaded up front.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Auto Height with SSRM" name="auto-height-ssrm" /%}

## Auto Height in a Detached Container

1. Open [/examples/grid-size-test/auto-height-detached/vanilla](/examples/grid-size-test/auto-height-detached/vanilla)
2. Click "Measure detached"
3. Less than 100 rows should be rendered or have getRowHeight called for them (the data set has 200 rows)
